  "id": "sacramento",
  "intro": "Sacramento sits in the flattest place in California, which makes it the best VHF ground in the state. From the levees there is nothing between you and the Coast Range in one direction or the Sierra foothills in the other, and handheld simplex behaves in a way it never does in the Bay Area. It is also the state capital, so the federal and state agency presence is heavy, and the Delta immediately south is a genuine inland waterway with its own marine traffic.",
  "introz": "萨克拉门托位于加州最平坦的地带，也因此是全州最好的 VHF 地形。站在河堤上，一侧到海岸山脉、另一侧到内华达山麓之间毫无遮挡，手台直通的表现和湾区完全不是一回事。这里还是州府，联邦和州级机构密集；南面紧邻的三角洲是一条真正的内陆水道，有自己的船舶通信。",
